#: renderers/web-components/src/functions/buildRegisterContext.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# Function: buildRegisterContext()"
msgstr "# Funktion: buildRegisterContext()"

#: renderers/web-components/src/functions/buildRegisterContext.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Build the shared [RegisterContext](../interfaces/RegisterContext.md) a `register()`-style call threads to every element's\n`define`. The icon resolver is injectable: `register()` always passes the real,\n`@pantoken/icons`-backed [iconSvg](iconSvg.md) (unchanged default behavior for every existing caller),\nwhile the per-element CDN build passes [noopIconSvg](noopIconSvg.md) for elements that never call it —\n`@pantoken/icons`/`@pantoken/tokens` is a multi-MB dependency, and since Rollup can't code-split\n`iife`/`umd` output, anything statically reachable from a bundle's entry ends up in the whole\nbundle, regardless of whether that specific element's code path ever invokes it. This module has no\ntop-level side effects for exactly that reason — importing it (unlike importing `../index.ts`, which\nauto-registers everything on import) never reaches [iconSvg](iconSvg.md) unless the caller passes it in."
msgstr "Byg den delte [RegisterContext](../interfaces/RegisterContext.md), som et `register()`-stil kald tråder til hvert elements\n`define`. Ikonoprøseren er injicerbar: `register()` sender altid den rigtige,\n`@pantoken/icons`-understøttet [iconSvg](iconSvg.md) (uændret standardadfærd for hver eksisterende opkalds),\nmedens per-element CDN-bygget sender [noopIconSvg](noopIconSvg.md) for elementer, der aldrig kalder det —\n`@pantoken/icons`/`@pantoken/tokens` er en multi-MB-afhængighed, og da Rollup ikke kan kode-splitte\n`iife`/`umd` output, noget statisk tilgængeligt fra en bundt's indgang ender i hele\nbundtet, uanset om det specifikke elements kodesti nogensinde kalder det. Dette modul har ingen\ntop-niveau bivirkninger af netop den grund — import af det (i modsætning til import af `../index.ts`, som\nauto-registrerer alt ved import) når aldrig [iconSvg](iconSvg.md) medmindre opkaldende sender det ind."

#: renderers/web-components/src/functions/buildRegisterContext.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Same shape as `register()`'s options, minus `only`."
msgstr "Samme form som `register()`'s muligheder, minus `only`."

#: renderers/web-components/src/functions/buildRegisterContext.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The registry to define into."
msgstr "Registret, der skal defineresind i."

#: renderers/web-components/src/functions/buildRegisterContext.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "### resolveIconSvg"
msgstr "### resolveIconSvg"

#: renderers/web-components/src/functions/buildRegisterContext.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The resolver wired into `ctx.iconSvg` — pass [iconSvg](iconSvg.md) for real icons\n  or [noopIconSvg](noopIconSvg.md) when the caller's element set provably never renders one (see\n  `ICON_ELEMENTS` in `./elements-meta.ts`)."
msgstr "Resolveren tilsluttet `ctx.iconSvg` — send [iconSvg](iconSvg.md) til rigtige ikoner\n  eller [noopIconSvg](noopIconSvg.md) når opkaldendes elementsæt pålideligt aldrig gengiver en (se\n  `ICON_ELEMENTS` i `./elements-meta.ts`)."

